# Model routing

Code never names a provider (no "gemini", "gpt-", "claude-" strings in application code).
Every model call goes through the LiteLLM proxy using a logical alias. Swapping the
underlying model is a gateway config change, not a code diff.

| Alias | Used for |
|---|---|
| `reasoning-high` | Story planning (4-beat arc), critique/QC judgement calls |
| `reasoning-fast` | Routing, classification, lightweight extraction |
| `vision-default` | Frame inspection, continuity QC scoring against the bible |
| `embed-default` | Any embeddings (not currently required by Video Agent v1 — see ADR-0005) |
| `realtime-voice` | Not used by Video Agent v1 (no dialogue/voiceover — out of scope) |

If a task seems to need a model capability not in this table, that's a signal to add an
alias at the gateway and document it here — not to call a provider SDK directly.
